\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Dollar Steady Against Yen as China Data Helps Spur Risk Appetite\b0\par\par\uc2 709 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2013\par 08:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Korean Newswires English Content\par \uc2 RTNWK\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Dollar hovers near Y99\par \par \uc2 --Strong Asian shares, Chinese data lift risk appetite\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar takes hit after RBN governor talks of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Alexander Martin\par \par \uc2 The dollar hovered around the Y99 level during Asian trading Wednesday, as strong Japanese share prices and better-than-expected Chinese data helped lift risk appetite.\par \par \uc2 Asian stock markets rallied on the back of a fresh record high Tuesday for the \uc2 Dow Jones Industrial\uc2  Average, with the Nikkei Stock Average up 1.4% at midday.\par \par \uc2 "Strong Asian share prices have helped lift the dollar/yen after it fell toward the mid Y98 level earlier in the session," said Kengo Suzuki, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Mizuho Securities\uc2  in Tokyo. But as the Nikkei began paring some of its earlier gains in afternoon trading, the dollar also seemed to be edging lower aginst the yen, he added.\par \par \uc2 As of 0450 GMT, the dollar was at Y98.96 from Y99.00 in late New York trading Tuesday. It briefly climbed to Y99.16, having fallen as low as Y98.63 earlier in the morning.\par \par \uc2 Traders and analysts said a large amount of selling orders around Y99.50 will serve as a heavy cap on the pair, and it may take some time before the dollar can breach the key Y100 level.\par \par \uc2 "Both the upside and downside of the dollar/yen appear limited. Another dose of strong U.S. data may be necessary to lift the pair higher," said Minori Uchida, chief analyst at the \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ. He said next week's U.S. retail sales data would be closely watched for cues.\par \par \uc2 Junichi Ishikawa, market analyst at IG Securities in Tokyo, said that while better-than-expected U.S. labor market data last week saw the dollar rally, it wasn't enough to clear all uncertainty over a U.S. economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 "The market is probably assuming it can embark on further dollar buying after the release of major economic indicators from next week onwards," he said.\par \par \uc2 Stronger-than-expected Chinese trade data also helped lift risk appetite, pushing up the Australian dollar, which fell Tuesday after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  lowered its benchmark interest rate.\par \par \uc2 China posted an $18.16 billion trade surplus in April, higher than a median forecast of $15.55 billion in a Dow Jones Newswires survey of economists. The Australian dollar climbed to $1.0194 from $1.0172 after the release of the data. As of 0450 GMT it was at $1.0187 from $1.0185, while the euro was at $1.3094 from $1.3079, and Y129.59 from Y129.48.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar fell after Reserve Bank of New Zealand Gov. \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2  reportedly said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the Kiwi to weaken it and is capable of doing so again to protect economic growth.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Dollar Index, which measures the dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at around 73.648 from 73.678.\par \par \uc2 Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Rates At 0150 EDT / 0450 GMT \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                              Latest       Previous   %Chg    Daily    Daily   %Chg \par    Dollar Rates                             Close             High     Low    12/31 \par    USD/JPY Japan            98.94-95       98.98-09  -0.06    99.14    98.66 +14.06 \par    EUR/USD Euro            1.3093-94      1.3077-80  +0.11   1.3097   1.3074  -