\par\par \b \uc2 DJ New Zealand Dollar Steadies; Euro Climbs On Strong German Data\b0\par\par\uc2 840 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2013\par 13:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Newswires English Content\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar steadies after RBNZ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  admission triggers losses overnight\par \par \uc2 -- Euro rallies after German industrial production rose in March economists had expected a decline\par \par \uc2 -- Norwegian, \uc2 Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate decisions due later Wednesday\par \par \uc2 By Jessica Mead\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar settled near its weakest levels for the month Wednesday after suffering heavy losses overnight on the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's admission it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent further \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength, while the euro rallied after better-than-expected German industrial production data.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar, or Kiwi, had tumbled almost a cent against the U.S. dollar in Asian trading hours to $0.8361 after RBNZ Governor \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and would do so again to contain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has risen about 10% over the past year against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Given the recent strong performance of the Kiwi, market participants believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were small in size.\par \par \uc2 "The takeaway from the RBNZ is that its pain thresholds for New Zealand dollar appreciation have been reached, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to step up its resistance by threatening rate cuts and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in our view," said strategists at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 In European hours, the Kiwi stabilized at around the $0.84 level with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists skeptical that this has marked the start of more frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , citing Mr. Wheeler's comments that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would expect to take the tops off rallies rather than materially change the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think we are going to see [the New Zealand dollar] tumble further. People have been buying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for diversification purposes, for yield. And as long as they are in that mindset, then they will still be buying it," said \uc2 Jane Foley\uc2  senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  in London, adding that it appears the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  just wants to take the edge off the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains.\par \par \uc2 The euro notched up gains after German March industrial production rose 1.2% on the month, confounding expectations for a 0.2% decline. The common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied to as high as $1.3148 against the dollar and nudged briefly back above Y130 against the yen.\par \par \uc2 The figures are the second successive positive surprise for the economy, following Tuesday's publication of much stronger-than-expected manufacturing orders for March.\par \par \uc2 In the session ahead, few data releases are scheduled and the focus will be on the Polish and Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate decisions.\par \par \uc2 The Polish rate decision is usually announced around 1100 GMT and most economists think the \uc2 Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will leave borrowing costs unchanged at 3.25% after the half-point cut in March. Some, however, are calling for a quarter-point cut and others, such as \uc2 Barclays\uc2 , are expecting another half-a-point cut.\par \par \uc2 The Norwegian decision is due at 1200 GMT. It is widely expected that the \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  will keep rates on hold at 1.5% for the seventh consecutive meeting, although some economists anticipate the bank mirroring the recent rate cut by the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At 1017 GMT, the euro was trading at $1.3139 against the dollar, compared with $1.3079 late Tuesday in New York, according to trading system EBS. The dollar was at Y98.94 against the yen, compared with Y99.00, while the euro was at Y129.96 compared with Y129.47. Meanwhile, the pound was trading at $1.5502 against the dollar, compared with $1.5485 late Tuesday in New York.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Dollar Index, which tracks the dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was trading at 73.514, compared with 73.678 late Tuesday in New York.\par \par \uc2 A summary of key levels for chart-watching technical strategists is below: \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/USD    USD/JPY    GBP/USD    USD/CHF \par Spot 1018 GMT     1.3136     98.94      1.5501     0.9389 \par 3 Day Trend       Range      Bearish    Bearish    Bullish \par Weekly Trend      Bullish    Range      Bullish    Range \par 200 day ma        1.3041     89.03      1.5625     0.9345 \par 3rd Resistance    1.3220     99.95      1.5556     0.9458 \par 2nd Resistance    1.3180     99.45      1.5540     0.9437 \par 1st Resistance    1.3160     99.16      1.5525     0.9420 \par Pivot*            1.3093     99.09      1.5494     0.9403 \par 1st S