\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand \highlight\uc2  Dollar Down Late as RBNZ Governor Mentions  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lucy Craymer   \par \uc2 415 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2013\par 07:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON--The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was lower late Wednesday following Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2 's confirmation of some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," but moves were pared by traders who decided it was more leaning than \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar fell sharply to US$0.8361 around 0050 GMT from about US$0.8460 after Mr. Wheeler told a parliamentary committee that "we've indicated on the record that we are prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange rate. We have also indicated that we would not expect, given the strength of the flows, that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would materially change the level of the exchange rate, but we could take potentially the tops of rallies. And in terms of activity, there has been some."\par \par \uc2 However, the sharp fall was somewhat reversed as market players mulled over the news and decided it wasn't significant \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market but only the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ongoing policy to lean against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been "steadily selling small amounts of the New Zealand dollar against notably the U.S. dollar," said ANZ Senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Manager Sam Tuck. "We haven't got the April number but we don't expect it to be much larger than any of the prior months."\par \par \uc2 In December the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 199 million New Zealand dollars after selling NZ$64 million in November. The two sales marked the first significant moves by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  since mid-2008.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also been grappling with an elevated Kiwi--up around 10% in the past year on a trade-weighted index basis--that is making it more difficult for companies in the country, which mostly exports agricultural products, to compete in global markets.\par \par \uc2 At 0530 GMT, the New Zealand dollar was trading around US$0.8398 compared with US$0.8497 late Tuesday. It was at A$0.8248 late in New Zealand from A$0.8337 late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Wednesday Mr. Wheeler said at the release of the Financial Stability Report that the New Zealand dollar was "over valued... perhaps significantly" and that it could continue appreciating which is a "significant concern."\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand April 2015 government bond fell 1 basis points to end at 2.45% and the April 2023 bond was unchanged at 3.20%.\par \par \uc2 Write to Lucy Craymer at lucy.craymer@wsj.com [ 08-05-13 0556GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1062 20711 4171   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130508e9580008n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
