\par\par \b \uc2 New Zealand Dollar Weakens; RBNZ Says  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  'Over-Valued'\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rebecca Howard   \par \uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2013\par 06:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON--The New Zealand dollar ended lower late Wednesday after taking a tumble when the Reserve Bank of New Zealand Governor \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is significantly over-valued and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stands ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At 0536 GMT, the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was trading at US$0.8409, after touching an intraday low of US$0.8394 following the speech. It was buying US$0.8439 late Tuesday. Against the Australian dollar it was at A$0.8113 versus A$0.8170 late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "There are no simple solutions available to the \uc2 Reserve Bank\uc2  on the exchange rate challenges we face," Mr. Wheeler told the manufacturers and exporters association in Auckland. "The Bank will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when circumstances are right. We will use the Official Cash Rate as circumstances require," he added.\par \par \uc2 Western Union\uc2  Business Solutions Corporate Dealing Manager Chris Hunter said, however, he expects the dip to be short-lived as the market will likely shrug off the comments. "There's no real change to the bank's stance here," he said. He said the Kiwi has short term support at US$0.8372 and resistance at US$0.8440.\par \par \uc2 In the longer term, traders expect the Kiwi to remain supported, in particular given strong dairy prices. BNZ \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategist Kymberly Martin noted that the latest GlobalDairyTrade auction, which took place overnight Tuesday, showed average milk prices up 3.1% since the prior auction two weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 "This was a very strong result, taking prices to +8.9% since the start of the year. This is in line with our broader view that positive New Zealand commodity price trends should help underpin the NZD this year," she said.\par \par \uc2 Dairy is the backbone of the New Zealand economy, representing around 25% of the island nation's NZ$46 billion of exports in the 12 months to the end of December.\par \par \uc2 Write to Rebecca Howard at rebecca.howard@wsj.com [ 20-02-13 0557GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1062 20711 4171   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130220e92k0005l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
