\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-NZ dollar overvalued, but no quick fixes to lower it - RBNZ\b0\par\par\uc2 561 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2013\par 03:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * NZ dollar overvalued, but no quick fixes - RBNZ governor\par \par \uc2 * RBNZ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  possible if conditions right\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely short term effect, QE won't work\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, comments, market reaction)\par \par \uc2 By Gyles Beckford\par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, Feb 20 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar is significantly overvalued compared with its economic fundamentals, but there are no quick means to bringing it down, including \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Wednesday, skittling the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by nearly half a cent.\par \par \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand Governor \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2  said part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength reflected global imbalances, a weak U.S. dollar, and New Zealand's improved terms of trade, but he said there were no simple solutions, including \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Given the strength of recent capital flows, we can only attempt to smooth the peaks of the USD/NZD exchange rate; we cannot determine the level," Wheeler said in a speech to a business group.\par \par \uc2 He said the RBNZ had four criteria for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- whether the exchange rate was at an exceptional level, whether it was justified, whether \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be consistent with monetary policy, and whether it was likely to succeed.\par \par \uc2 However, he said it was unlikely to have a sustained impact in bringing down the exchange rate but it could ease pressures in the short term.\par \par \uc2 "When the NZ dollar is coming under upward pressure, we want investors to know that the Kiwi is not a one way bet," Wheeler said.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar fell nearly half a cent to a low of $0.8411 after Wheeler's comments.\par \par \uc2 It also lost ground on cross rates against the Australia dollar, euro, and yen, sending the trade weighted New Zealand dollar index, the RBNZ's preferred \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  measure, down around 0.6 percent, after hitting a post-float high last week.\par \par \uc2 "He said that he was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if required, but he added that four criteria have to be met, and they're certainly not met yet," said Tim Kelleher, head of institutional sales at ASB Bank.\par \par \uc2 The kiwi, along with the neighbouring Aussie and other commodity linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , have risen strongly this year, as central banks have effectively printed money, lowering their exchange rates, in a bid to stimulate their economies.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  and the \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  called for members to allow market determined exchange rates.\par \par \uc2 Wheeler reiterated previous comments that quantitative easing measures as practised by some economies would unlikely to be successful in New Zealand.\par \par \uc2 "Quantitative easing would increase inflation, raise inflation expectations, stimulate asset prices, and lead eventually to higher interest rates," Wheeler said, adding that a Switzerland-style capping of the New Zealand dollar would be highly inflationary.\par \par \uc2 The full text of the speech is available at:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.rbnz.govt.nz/speeches/5150125.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.rbnz.govt.nz/speeches/5150125.html}}}\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Bill English last week dismissed the idea of cutting rates or directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, saying \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  was too small and should not risk its limited funds.\par \par \uc2 Wheeler also repeated that New Zealand needed to improve productivity, reduce foreign borrowing, sort out distortions in saving and investment incentives, and cut fiscal imbalances.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Jacqueline Wong)\par \par \uc2 NEWZEALAND-ECONOMY/RBNZ (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | M | ND | E | RBN | ABX | AFA | CSA | LBY | RWSA | RWS | REULB | GNS | RNP | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130220e92k0003b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
