\par\par \b \uc2 New Zealand Dollar Down Late But Consolidating, Eyes On US GDP\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rebecca Howard   \par \uc2 415 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2012\par 06:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON--The New Zealand dollar was slightly lower late Friday but was consolidating after falling in the wake of a speech by Reserve Bank Governor \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Wheeler told the Admirals' Breakfast Club in Auckland in a speech Friday that price stability and financial stability remained the \uc2 Reserve Bank\uc2 's central objectives for monetary and prudential policy, and this had been reinforced by the newly signed Policy Targets Agreement.\par \par \uc2 However, the Kiwi took a tumble after Mr. Wheeler retained the possibility of a cut to the official cash rate. He also said while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would like to see a lower exchange rate, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to have a sustainable effect on the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. However, "the bank will remain vigilant on its criteria for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and will be prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if all its conditions are met," said Mr. Wheeler.\par \par \uc2 The RBNZ last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in June 2007 and its policy only allows for it to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is deemed to be exceptionally high or low; when it believes the exchange rate is unjustifiable by economic fundamentals; where \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is consistent with the PTA; and where markets are such that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a reasonable chance of success.\par \par \uc2 HiFX\uc2  Senior Trader Stuart Ive said he was surprised by the market reaction as Mr. Wheeler's speech seems to indicate he is not out there "to rock the boat" and is going to keep policies steady as they go, said Mr. Ive.\par \par \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategist Sue Trinh says the speech didn't change the market's view and she is still expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain on hold until 2014. She says the Kiwi is consolidating around the current levels after a recent run-up in risk. Ms. Trinh says the market is now focusing on the U.S. gross domestic product data and consumer confidence survey due later in the global trading day.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar was buying around US$0.8184 a 0351 GMT, versus US$0.8221 late Thursday. The Kiwi was buying A$0.7926 versus A$0.7935. The April 2015 bond was 1.5 basis points lower at 2.59%, while the April 2023s ended down 2 basis points at 3.565%.\par \par \uc2 Write to Rebecca Howard at rebecca.howard@wsj.com [ 26-10-12 0402GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1062 20711 4171   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121026e8aq0005y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
