\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ RBNZ Governor Wheeler: Price, Financial Stability Remain Central Objectives\b0\par\par\uc2 399 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2012\par 22:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 25 Oct 2012 16:04 EDT *DJ  RBNZ Wheeler: RBNZ Places High Priority On Strengthening NZ's Prudential Regime\par \par \uc2 25 Oct 2012 16:04 EDT *DJ  RBNZ Wheeler: New Zealand Doesn't Require Quantitative Easing\par \par \uc2 25 Oct 2012 16:05 EDT *DJ  RBNZ Wheeler: RBNZ Has Scope To Lower Interest Rates If Needed\par \par \uc2 25 Oct 2012 16:06 EDT *DJ  RBNZ Wheeler: Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Is Unlikely To Have Sustainable Impact On Kiwi\par \par \uc2 25 Oct 2012 16:08 EDT *DJ  RBNZ Wheeler: Need to Alter Country's Saving, Investment Pattern if to Lower NZD\par \par \uc2 25 Oct 2012 16:11 EDT *DJ  RBNZ Wheeler Speaking At the Admiral's Breakfast Club In Auckland\par \par \uc2 25 Oct 2012 16:38 EDT DJ  RBNZ Wheeler: RBNZ Prepared To \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  If Conditions Are Met\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Lucy Craymer \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WELLINGTON--\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Reserve Bank Governor Graeme Wheeler said Thursday that "the bank will remain vigilant on its criteria for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and will be prepared to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " in the market to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar "if all its conditions are met."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Wheeler added in a speech to the Admiral's Breakfast Club in Auckland that the Reserve Bank would like to see a lower New Zealand dollar "provided it could be achieved without damaging price and financial stability," but \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets is unlikely to have a sustainable effect on the New Zealand dollar in the long term.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "New Zealand is one of several countries that have experienced upward pressure on its exchange rate in recent years. Ultimately it is the relative rates of return between New Zealand and the rest of the world that explains the strength of the New Zealand dollar," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He added that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  didn't need to pursue a policy of quantitative easing as the economy is growing at an annual rate of around 2%, but the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\f28 \uc2 \f2  had the scope to lower interest rates if needed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Wheeler said price stability and financial stability remain the Reserve Bank's central objectives for monetary policy and prudential policy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "These provide the best framework for achieving stronger growth in output and employment in the longer term," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Lucy Craymer at lucy.craymer@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 25, 2012 16:38 ET (20:38 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020121025e8ap007er\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
