\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-UPDATE 1-New RBNZ head backs inflation goal, douses  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk\b0\par\par\uc2 566 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2012\par 01:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Corrects spelling of "head" in headline)\par \par \uc2  * Inflation, financial system focus of policy\par \par \uc2  * Says while NZ$ high, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap it would not work\par \par \uc2  * Approach seen signalling no major changes \par \par \uc2  By Naomi Tajitsu\par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON, Oct 26 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  is focused on keeping inflation in check and the financial system healthy, prerequisites for a stronger economy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new governor said on Friday as he doused expectations of measures to lower the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2  made the comments in his first public speech as governor, a day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held the official cash rate (OCR) at a record-low 2.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  "Price stability and financial stability remain the \uc2 Reserve Bank\uc2 's central objectives for monetary policy and prudential policy," said Wheeler, who took over from Alan Bollard at the end of last month.\par \par \uc2  "Our economy is growing at an annual rate of around 2 percent and the \uc2 Reserve Bank\uc2  has scope to lower interest rates if needed," he said, but added it was not the role of monetary policy to target growth rates.\par \par \uc2  One analyst said the speech showed there would not be any major surprises from a Wheeler-led \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  "He is not going to revamp the monetary policy framework or introduce quantitative easing and declare a futile war on the exchange rate," ANZ senior economist \uc2 Mark Smith\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2  Wheeler said the economy would benefit from a lower exchange rate if it could be achieved without compromising other policy goals, and so while lower interest rates might initially push down the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  there was unlikely to be a sustained impact.\par \par \uc2  "If we reduced the OCR without sound reasons, the exchange rate might drop initially but rise later when the inflationary implications of the rate cut became clear," Wheeler said.\par \par \uc2  The New Zealand dollar has gained around 10 percent since hitting its low point for the year in early June. \par \par \uc2  CLEAR CRITERIA\par \par \uc2  The RBNZ had clear criteria for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including whether it would work, whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was exceptionally high, and whether the market conditions were right -- and Wheeler indicated those conditions had not been met.\par \par \uc2  "It makes little sense to risk incurring losses to taxpayers by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  when \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar are particularly strong."\par \par \uc2  Wheeler also dismissed the practicality of capital controls, saying they would damage the credibility and stability of the financial sector, and increase the real cost of capital.\par \par \uc2  The kiwi dollar fell nearly half a cent to a low of $0.8159 after the comments, before settling back around $0.8190.\par \par \uc2  Wheeler said his policy agreement with the government had reinforced the importance of controlling inflation, in particular aiming for the mid-point of the 1-3 percent target band.\par \par \uc2  "Over time, attaining this outcome should help to anchor inflation expectations around the mid-point."\par \par \uc2  He noted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also had macro-prudential tools, such as core funding ratios, capital buffers, sectoral risk weights, and housing loan-to-value ratio limits, to deal with  any inflation bubbles that developed.\par \par \uc2  Quantitative easing of the sort undertaken in the United States, Europe, and Japan were not needed in New Zealand, he said.     \par \par \uc2 (Editing by John Mair and Paul Tait)\par \par \uc2 NEWZEALAND-ECONOMY/RBNZ  (UPDATE 1, CORRECTED) | ABX | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | ND | RNP | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121025e8ap001u8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
