\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ NZ Fin Min: Talks With Central Bankers Confirmed View, Costs, Risks of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  High\b0\par\par\uc2 676 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2012\par 06:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 13 Oct 2012 00:09 EDT *DJ  NZ Fin Min: Worried About Central Banks Unwinding Positions After Monetary Easing\par \par \uc2 13 Oct 2012 00:10 EDT DJ  INTERVIEW: NZ Fin Min Says Costs, Risks of \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  'Very High'\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  finance minister says talks with central bankers confirmed view that costs, risks of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  high\par \par \uc2 --Says worried about central banks unwinding positions after monetary easing \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Eleanor Warnock and Ainsley Thomson \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO--New Zealand Finance Minister Bill English said discussions in recent days with countries that have in the past \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reaffirmed his belief that a similar tactic was the wrong strategy for New Zealand.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's confirmed for me that the costs and risks of it [\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ] are very high, particularly for a small open economy," Mr. English, who is in Tokyo for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 World Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  annual meetings, said in an interview.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He said during his time in Tokyo, he had spoken with a former governor of Switzerland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the current governor of Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Masaaki Shirakawa. Both countries have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the past to weaken their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Since the beginning of 2009, the New Zealand dollar has appreciated about 40% against the U.S. dollar. The New Zealand dollar, which reached a post-float high of US$0.8841 in August 2011, was at US$0.8170 at Friday's market close.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's economy is heavily dependent on trade, and a stronger dollar has put a pinch on the nation's exporters by making products more expensive abroad.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. English said his country's strategy to deal with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issue would be centered on increasing the competitiveness of its exporters, and expressed hope that the agricultural-product heavy makeup of its exports would make it better positioned to withstand a slowdown in China than its neighbor Australia, which exports large amounts of minerals and energy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "A slowdown (in China) would affect us, but we're reasonably optimistic that in the long run demand for our food and protein products is likely to be steady and growing," he said. "Over a longer period our prices will be a bit less volatile (than Australia) because we're geared into the growing middle-class in China rather than the infrastructure side."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 More than a third of the value of the country's exports were dairy and meat products in the year ended Sept. 30, 2011, according to government statistics.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. English added that this week's meetings had also raised the question of the world's central banks unwinding their positions after taking strong monetary easing measures in recent years.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I don't think we really understand the unwinding of these extraordinary monetary measures. That's all out ahead of us," he said. "Demographics are going to be pushing a lot of people to cash in their assets. Baby boomers are going to be selling and so are the central banks and it may not be as politically straight forward as it looks now."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We are pleased to be in an economy where those innovative monetary tools haven't been used," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand dollar has also gained on safe haven flows from investors fleeing turmoil in Europe, and looking for higher returns than in other developed countries where interest rates have dropped to historical lows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commenting on a possible reversal of safe-haven flows after a return of global investor confidence, Mr. English said: "That would help our rebalancing, which we need to do. That would be a good problem to have."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But he added that "there doesn't look to me to be a turning point in the near term."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Eleanor Warnock at eleanor.warnock@dowjones.com and Ainsley Thomson at ainsley.thomson@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribe to WSJ: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 13, 2012 00:10 ET (04:10 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020121013e8ad00093\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
