\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW: N.Z. Fin Min:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  to Lower Exchange Rate Not a Solution\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ainsley Thomson  \par \uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2012\par 20:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Asian Equities Report\par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON--Recent moves by the world's largest central banks to stimulate their economies is driving up the New Zealand dollar and making life harder for the country's exporters, but \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to lower the exchange rate isn't a solution, New Zealand Finance Minister Bill English said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 "We don't see a simple or easy way to manipulate the exchange rate," Mr. English said in an interview with Dow Jones Newswires. "Those countries that have set out to do so are either not succeeding or exposing themselves to pretty large risks."\par \par \uc2 Mr. English, who is in London to meet with U.K. Chancellor of the Exchequer \uc2 George Osborne\uc2 , international investors and rating agencies, said the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has authority to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in specific circumstances--when there is extreme market disorder or to trim peaks and troughs in the exchange-rate cycle.\par \par \uc2 "It's up to them to decide whether those conditions apply, but we don't intend to create the expectation that somehow the N.Z. government can pick the exchange rate and push the market in that direction," he said.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar, which reached a post-float high of US$0.8841 in August 2011, is currently trading around US$0.8202.\par \par \uc2 Like Australia and emerging-market countries such as Brazil, New Zealand has seen its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthen as result of moves by central banks in major economies--such as the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  and the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 --to ease their respective monetary policies. Investors are flocking to countries and assets that offer higher interest rates than the low rates offered in Japan, the U.S. and parts of Europe.\par \par \uc2 That, in turn, is prompting other central banks to employ their own measures to depreciate their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. English, who is a lawmaker in the center-right National party that has governed since 2008, said rather than \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the government is trying to improve the competitiveness of exporters--a policy he conceded would take time to make an impact.\par \par \uc2 Mr. English criticized the monetary policy tool of quantitative easing--in which a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  effectively prints more money to buy bonds--labelling it an "extreme measure".\par \par \uc2 "It's my view that while printing money has some shorter-term benefits, there is a lot of uncertainty about the longer-term damage that is being done," he said. "I'm pleased that we're not involved in that kind of process."\par \par \uc2 Mr. English said the most recent forecasts show the government is on track to achieve a budget surplus in the year to June 2015, but he said there were indications the economy had softened since then.\par \par \uc2 "We have a bit of headroom built into those last forecasts," he said, "but the way the world is changing, you take it one at a time."\par \par \uc2 Mr. English said an economic slowdown in China was a concern because of the impact it would have on Australia, which is New Zealand's largest market.\par \par \uc2 "How we do will depend more on impacts of the U.S. drought on dairy prices than whether China is up or down another percentage point," he said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. English said the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2 's decision Tuesday to cut its benchmark lending rate by 0.25 percentage point to 3.25%, was a reminder that Australia's once-in-a-hundred-year mining investment boom wouldn't last forever.\par \par \uc2 -Rebecca Howard in Wellington contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ainsley Thomson at ainsley.thomson@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Subscribe to WSJ: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires }}}\uc2  [ 03-10-12 1831GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument AER0000020121003e8a300018\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
