\par\par \b \uc2 Soggy euro and firmer stocks lift Aussie & kiwi dlrs\b0\par\par\uc2 461 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2012\par 04:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON/SYDNEY, Sept 21 (Reuters) - The Australian and New Zealand dollars rose against a broadly soggy euro on Friday and firmed against the U.S. dollar as well, but the high-beta \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were seen vulnerable to renewed concerns about the global growth outlook.\par \par \uc2 * The euro skids to its weakest in one week at A$1.2391\par \par \uc2 and NZ$1.5610, well off three-month peaks hit on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 * Euro got stung overnight after a batch of surveys showed euro zone business activity remained weak despite the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent bold plans aimed at tackling the region's debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 * Decent size euro selling also helps lifts the Antipodeans against the greenback, with the Aussie up 0.3 pct on the day at $1.0465.\par \par \uc2 * The Aussie has bounced from a low of $1.0367 overnight, but remains well off a five-month high of $1.0625 hit Friday. It is showing a loss of nearly one percent for the week.\par \par \uc2 * The New Zealand dollar edges up to a session high of $0.8306, but its upside is capped as traders suspect offers into $0.8310. The kiwi has failed to make headway beyond $0.8300 in the past few days. Still, it is among the best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , having risen nearly three cents in two weeks.\par \par \uc2 * Antipodeans getting support from upbeat equities across Asia. The improving mood is squeezing Aussie shorts with traders citing stops above $1.0500. Sellers are camped around $1.0475.\par \par \uc2 * A clean break below $1.0400 would target $1.0340, the 61.8 percent retracement of the move from $1.0165 to $1.0625.\par \par \uc2 * NZ \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  outperforms Aussie, which sinks to a five-month low around NZ$1.2560.\par \par \uc2 * Kiwi on track to end the week unchanged vs the U.S. dollar. It got a lift after a surprisingly strong reading of New Zealand growth on Thursday indicating the nation is chugging along even as many major economies continue to struggle.\par \par \uc2 * Local lawmakers have been increasing pressure on the New Zealand government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the kiwi, which has strengthened against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to its yield advantage.\par \par \uc2 * But the government is opposed to any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the \uc2 Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to test the market.\par \par \uc2 * New Zealand government bonds slip, pushing yields 2 basis points higher at the short end of the curve.\par \par \uc2 * Australian debt futures are also under pressure, with the three-year contract down 0.06 points at 97.440, while the 10-year contract is off 0.05 points at 96.815.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-AUSTRALIA-NEWZEALAND/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  | AUF | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | ND | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120924e89l0002f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
