\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ NZ PM Says NZD/USD Overvalued But Doesn't Believe  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Can Be Successful\b0\par\par\uc2 214 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2012\par 06:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 23 Apr 2012 00:51 EDT DJ  NZ PM Says NZD/USD Overvalued But Doesn't Believe \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Can Be Successful\par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Prime Minister John Key said Monday that he wouldn't support the Reserve Bank Of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, even though he sees the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar as overvalued.\par \par \uc2 "I don't believe in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I never have and, frankly, I never will," Key said at a press conference.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar fell last week after Key was reported to have said the government was looking at ways to moderate the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Key said the New Zealand government would continue to keep its spending under control to reduce the work of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Dreaming that we can somehow get the exchange rate under control through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is la-la-land stuff," he said.\par \par \uc2 He added that a high New Zealand dollar wasn't all bad as it did keep inflation under control and therefore reduced pressure on the RBNZ.\par \par \uc2 -By Lucy Craymer, Dow Jones Newswires; +64-4-471-5990; lucy.craymer@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 23, 2012 00:51 ET (04:51 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120423e84n0036g\par }\page {\