\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For April 23\b0\par\par\uc2 1,779 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2012\par 09:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: INITIAL HSBC CHINA PMI GAINS IN APRIL BUT STILL IN CONTRACTIONARY RANGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An initial measure of China's manufacturing activity showed fresh signs of strength in April, but the data indicate the economy is still in sluggish territory and may need a government boost. (published 0542 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIA 1Q PPI FALL STRENGTHENS CASE FOR RATE CUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian wholesale prices recorded their biggest quarterly fall since late 2009 in the first quarter of 2012, increasing bets that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  will cut interest rates next week. (published 0347 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S BUDGET COULD FACE HURDLES AMID POLITICAL DRAMA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Prime Minister Julia Gillard could face a delicate balancing act in winning backing for the May budget amid a political drama that threatens the stability of her minority government. (published 0509 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC CHIEF: RISK FROM WIDENED YUAN TRADING BAND MANAGEABLE - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has a number of tools to manage its exchange rate and the risks from the yuan's newly widened trading band are manageable, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Zhou Xiaochuan was quoted as saying in a report. (published 0142 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SINGAPORE INFLATION JUMPS, KEEPING HEAT ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's consumer price index rose at a faster-than-expected pace in March, driven by a surge in costs of private road transport and housing, highlighting a stubborn inflation problem that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moved to tackle last week with a surprise tightening in monetary policy. (published 0626 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S&P AFFIRMS INDONESIA RATING AT BB+ WITH POSITIVE OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ratings Services affirmed its BB+ long-term sovereign credit rating of Indonesia, disappointing some who had thought the firm would follow the two other major rating companies in raising the country's government debt rating to investment grade. (published 0632 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: INDONESIA RECORDS 30.3% INCREASE IN FDI IN 1Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign direct investment in Indonesia rose by 30.3% in the first quarter from a year earlier to IDR51.5 trillion, the Investment Coordinating Board said Monday, as the country was boosted by two international credit rating firms' decision to raise Indonesia's rating to investment grade for the first time in 14 years. (published 0450 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: NZ PM SAYS KIWI OVERVALUED, BUT DOESN'T BELIEVE IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Prime Minister John Key said Monday he wouldn't support Reserve Bank Of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand intervenion\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, even though he sees the local dollar as overvalued. (published 0603 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN PM SAYS WOULD CONSIDER REDUCED SALES TAX RATES FOR SOME BASIC ITEMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Monday that he would consider lower sales tax rates on some basic items to lessen the burden of his proposed national tax hike. (published 0528 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ADB'S NAG: ASIAN MONETARY POLICY STANCES CURRENTLY APPROPRIATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian economies generally don't face any immediate inflation threat and their monetary policy stances are "about right" currently, managing director-general of the Asian Development Bank Rajat Nag said Monday. (published 0338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MOODY'S: RESERVE BANK OF INDIA EASING MEASURES ARE CREDIT POSITIVE FOR BANKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank Of India's recent interest-rate cut and increased liquidity support are credit positive for the country's banks at a time of rising pressures on liquidity and asset quality, analysts at Moody's Investors Service said Monday. (published 0436 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINES 1Q TAX COLLECTION PHP229.04 BLN, UP 15% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bureau of Internal Revenue, the Philippine government's main tax collection agency, said Monday it collected PHP229.04 billion in revenue during the first quarter, up 15% compared with the same period last year. (published 0428 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIETNAM APRIL CPI UP 0.05% ON MONTH, UP 10.54% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's consumer price index in April rose 0.05% from the previous month led by increases in the prices of transport and education services, government figures showed Monday. (published 0306 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: RBNZ TO STAND PAT; MAY ATTEMPT TO JAWBONE NZ DOLLAR LOWER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand is expected to leave the Official Cash Rate unchanged at 2.50% Thursday and may further soften its hiking bias due to the strength of the New Zealand dollar and subdued inflationary pressure. (published 0339 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 PFIZER\f28 \uc2 \f2  EXPECTED TO ANNOUNCE SALE OF INFANT-NUTRITION BUSINESS TO NESTLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pfizer Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is expected to announce on Monday it has reached a deal to sell its baby-food business to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nestle SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  for more than $10 billion, according to people familiar with the matter. (published 0406 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: COCKATOO COAL SAYS \f28 \uc2 \f2 SK NETWORKS\f28 \uc2 \f2  CANCELS PLANNED INVESTMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 SK Networks Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has backed out of a planned A$313 million investment in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cockatoo Coal Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . that would have given it a commanding 40% stake in the coal producer, the companies said in separate regulatory filings Monday. (published 0133 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S BIOTA PLANS TO MERGE WITH \f28 \uc2 \f2 NABI BIOPHARMACEUTICALS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Influenza drug developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Biota Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it aims to improve its value for shareholders by merging with U.S.-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nabi Biopharmaceuticals\f28 \uc2 \f2  to form a combined company, which it plans to list on Nasdaq. (published 0416 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SHANGHAI FOSUN PHARMACEUTICAL GETS HK REGULATOR'S OK FOR HK IPO - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shanghai Fosun Pharmaceutical Co. has received regulatory approval for its up to US$800 million Hong Kong initial public offering, a person familiar with the situation said Monday. (published 0149 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SAMVARDHANA MOTHERSON FINANCE IPO TO OPEN MAY 2, CLOSE MAY 4 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samvardhana Motherson Finance Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s initial public offering will open for subscriptions on May 2 and close on May 4, according to a \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bombay Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  regulatory filing Monday. (published 0338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: TOYOTA DEBUTS 2 NEW CONCEPT VEHICLES AT BEIJING MOTOR SHOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Monday unveiled a pair of new concept cars--a compact for global markets that will be sold in China from next year and a hybrid developed exclusively for China. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 JAPAN TOBACCO\f28 \uc2 \f2  REJIGS MANAGEMENT, NO EX-MOF OFFICIAL INCLUDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan Tobacco Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it is reshuffling top management so as not to have a former finance ministry official as either chairman or president for the first time since the company was privatized in 1985. (published 0623 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ORIGIN RAISES BASSGAS UPGRADE COST TO A$460M ON DELAYS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Origin Energy Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday the cost of an upgrade to its BassGas project, offshore Victoria state, has risen to A$460 million from A$360 million after delays caused by construction setbacks. (published 0216 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KRUNG THAI BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  1Q NET PROFIT THB6.38 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Krung Thai Bank PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Thailand's second-largest lender by assets, said Monday its first-quarter net profit rose 16.2% from a year earlier owing to higher interest and non-interest income. (published 0553 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FONTERRA CALLS SPECIAL MEETING FOR FINAL VOTE ON TRADING AMONG FARMERS SHARE PLAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's Fonterra Co-Operative Group Ltd. said Monday that it will hold a final vote on its Trading Among Farmers scheme at a special meeting June 25, in a bid to unify its shareholder base. (published 0326 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DONGYUE CANCELS PLANS TO SELL SHARES, BONDS; NO AGREEMENT ON TERMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese refrigerant manufacturer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dongyue Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has cancelled its plan to issue shares and bonds after it can't reach agreement with potential investors on the terms of its proposed issuance, the company said Monday. (published 0440 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par QANTAS CEO CALLS FOR SECOND SYDNEY AIRPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Qantas Airways Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s chief executive, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alan Joyce\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Monday said bottlenecks at Sydney airport were unsustainable and called for a second hub in the city before its global reputation was damaged. (published 0216 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DRB-HICOM: HAVEN'T DECIDED ON WHETHER TO SELL \f28 \uc2 \f2 LOTUS GROUP\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysian conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 DRB-HICOM Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it hasn't decided on whether to sell \f28 \uc2 \f2 Proton Holdings Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s U.K. sports-car unit, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lotus Group International Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0102 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TELECOM NZ: NEW CHIEF EXECUTIVE, MANAGING DIRECTOR WILL BE SIMON MOUTTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Simon Moutter will take over as chief executive and managing director of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Telecom Corp of New Zealand Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Sept. 1, the company said in a statement Monday. (published 2100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EDSERV: TO OFFER EDUCATION CONTENT ON AMAZON'S ONLINE STORE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EdServ Softsystems Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday said it has tied up with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Amazon.com Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to offer educational software applications and content on the U.S. company's online store. (published 0531 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY LOWER; CHINA PMI DATA FAIL TO SUPPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mostly lower Monday amid a lack of positive catalysts, while manufacturing data in China failed to dispel concerns of weakness in Asia's largest economy. (published 0430 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL DATA: CHINA CONFIRMS MARCH CRUDE-OIL IMPORTS UP 8.7% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Iranian crude oil imports were cut by more than half in March, data from China's General Administration of Customs showed Monday, after \f28 \uc2 \f2 China International United Petroleum & Chemical Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or Unipec, skipped shipments in February because of a commercial dispute with \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Iranian Oil Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0634 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA KNOC: JANUARY-MARCH IRAN CRUDE IMPORTS DOWN 22.3% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's imports of Iranian crude oil in the January-March period fell to 17.7 million barrels, a decline of 22.3% from the same period a year earlier, preliminary data from state-run \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korea National Oil Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . showed Monday. (published 0509 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: AUSTRALIAN 2012-13 CANOLA CROP COULD HIT NEW RECORD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 23-04-12 0707GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Last year we had a record crop by a long shot. We're reconciling the final numbers now but [it could be] somewhere between 3.0 million and 3.3 million tons...so it was bigger than expected," he told Dow Jones in an interview. (published 0423 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par COAL DATA: NEWCASTLE EXPORTS +6.62% ON WEEK AT 2.91 MLN TONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Coal export volumes from Australia's Newcastle port, the world's largest coal export terminal, rose 6.62% in the week ended April 23, data from the port authority showed. (published 0329 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA TRIBUNAL SCRAPS GREEN OK GIVEN TO \f28 \uc2 \f2 JINDAL STEEL\f28 \uc2 \f2  MINING PROJECT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's environmental and tribal activists have scored another victory over companies looking to start mining and related projects in the mineral-rich and densely forested regions of the country. (published 0533 GMT) [ 23-04-12 0707GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120423e84n000fy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
