\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Aussie, NZ dlrs to dip only modestly in 2012\b0\par\par\uc2 517 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2012\par 07:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * For results see and\par \par \uc2 By Cecile Lefort\par \par \uc2 SYDNEY, Feb 3 (Reuters) - The high-flying Australian and New Zealand dollars may pull back modestly in the coming months on global concerns, but will continue to be supported by their status as commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a Reuters poll showed.\par \par \uc2 The median forecast of more than 50 analysts polled by Reuters showed the Australian dollar gradually slipping to $1.015 in early 2013, although still above parity.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, it was up at $1.0680, having risen 5 percent so far this year. The Aussie and the New Zealand dollar, which is up 7 percent this year, are among the best performing major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in that period. See and for polls.\par \par \uc2 "Residual eurozone uncertainties, including the outcome of Greek PSI negotiations, and the pace/magnitude of recent gains lead us to expect NZD/USD and AUD/USD to be modestly lower," said Hamish Pepper, an analyst at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 A survey of 46 analysts showed the New Zealand dollar was also expected to gently pull back to $0.78 mid-year, from $0.8300 where it currently stands.\par \par \uc2 The Antipodean \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been in demand since the U.S. Federal Reserve pledged to keep rates near zero out to late 2014 and triggered expectations of more easing. This is encouraging investors to borrow in dollars to fund carry trades in commodities and higher yielding assets.\par \par \uc2 Investors have been piling on long positions even though the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  is almost certain to cut rates again next week partly because of global growth concerns as the European debt crisis drags on.\par \par \uc2 With a current cash rate at 4.25 percent, Australia has one of the highest rates in the developed world and has room to cut further should it need to stimulate growth, unlike many of its peers.\par \par \uc2 STRETCHED POSITIONS\par \par \uc2 Analysts warn, however, the Aussie bullish run could end abruptly.\par \par \uc2 "As these net long positions become increasingly stretched, at some stage there will be a downward correction to the Antipodeans \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and these players will likely become forced sellers," said Annette Beacher, head of Asia-Pacific research at \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 The kiwi has been a big favourite of momentum players and black box funds betting it can go a lot further yet, particularly as \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the yen and Swiss franc have been hemmed in by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Barclays\uc2 ' Pepper expected \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain its yield advantage over other G10 economies given a likely extended period of extremely low interest rates in the U.S. and eurozone.\par \par \uc2 He also forecast that the Reserve Bank of New Zealand (RBNZ) will start hiking rates in the second half of 2012.\par \par \uc2 The RBNZ held its cash rate at a record-low equalling 2.5 percent last week because of global outlook concerns and modest domestic growth. A majority of analysts forecast the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will tighten its monetary policy late this year or early 2013.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Cecile Lefort; Editing by Ramya Venugopal)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-AUSTRALIA-NEWZEALAND-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120203e823000ne\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
