\par\par \b \uc2 NZ Dollar Up Late, Firm Ahead Of FOMC Meeting\b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2010\par 05:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                           Late        Change \par  NZD/USD                 0.7664       +0.0125 \par  NZD/AUD                 0.7758       +0.0039 \par  NZD/JPY                 61.81        +1.075 \par  Nov 2011 Bond           3.59%        +3.0 bps \par  May 2021 Bond           5.285%       +5.0 bps \par  10-Year U.S. Spread     +266 bps     +14 bps \par  90-Day Bank Bill        3.19%        unchanged \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The New Zealand dollar traded at its highest level in 27 months against the U.S. dollar Monday as investors took positions ahead of the two-day U.S. Federal Reserve policy meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 At 0330 GMT, the New Zealand dollar was trading at US$0.7664, compared with US$0.7539 late Friday. It touched a high of US$0.7672.\par \par \uc2 "There is a truckload of event risk" that is likely to buffet the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with a string of policy meetings by other central banks through the week, Mike Symonds, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at BNZ, said.\par \par \uc2 A lot of attention will focus on the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  Tuesday, which is expected to keep interest rates on hold.\par \par \uc2 But Symonds said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has recently been in the habit of surprising financial markets.\par \par \uc2 Market pricing for a hike in Australia is around 20%, but Symonds says this is too low with the actual risk closer to 50%.\par \par \uc2 The RBA could easily choose to hike, moving preemptively to head off inflationary pressures next year. Even if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds its cash rate target at 4.5%, there is very little risk it will back away from its intention to eventually increase rates.\par \par \uc2 HIFX\uc2  senior trader Stuart Ive said that strong manufacturing data from China gave further support to the New Zealand dollar through the day.\par \par \uc2 Even a small pullback following rumors of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities to sell yen against the U.S. dollar only resulted in new attractive levels to buy the Kiwi. A Japanese government official said Monday that the yen's moves have been "excessive" recently, but declined to comment on whether Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is very resilient right now," Ive said.\par \par \uc2 But clear direction won't be restored until the "design and extent" of U.S. quantitative easing measures are announced, he said.\par \par \uc2 New Zealand government bonds were lower in price over the day in extremely thin trade, tracking moves in the swap rates curve.\par \par \uc2 One trader said moves were probably exaggerated as uncertainty will persist in the market until the Fed announces its policy measures.\par \par \uc2 -By James Glynn, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; james.glynn@dowjones.com [ 01-11-10 0425GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1062 20711 4171   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101101e6b1000a0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
