\par\par \b \uc2 NZ Dlr Sharply Weaker Late, Hurt By Rising Risk Aversion\b0\par\par\uc2 508 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 2008\par 05:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                           Late        Change \par  NZD/USD                  0.5279       -0.0136 \par  NZD/AUD                  0.8576       +0.0095 \par  NZD/JPY                  49.72        -2.13 \par  Nov 2011 Bond            4.945%       -14.5 bps \par  Dec 2017 Bond            5.405%       -18.5 bps \par  10-Year U.S. Spread      +236 bps     +11 bps \par  90-Day Bank Bill         5.785%        -2.5 bps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The New Zealand dollar was weaker late Friday, hammered by persistent weakness in global stock markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Early in the session, the Kiwi touched a six-year low of US$0.5193 as investors bailed out of high yielding, risky \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in favor of safe-haven assets.\par \par \uc2 It recovered slightly later in the day, helped by some profit-taking and a stronger Australian dollar after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  said it had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to "provide liquidity" to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 Traders said, however, that the bias for the Kiwi is definitely down.\par \par \uc2 The markets are being driven by "panic and fear" and "it's tough to see where any upside is going to come from," said OzForex dealer Jim Vrondas.\par \par \uc2 Early in the day, local traders said there were some rumors that the Reserve \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  was watching rates, and may be ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the Kiwi, although there was no concrete evidence.\par \par \uc2 HIFX trading director Mike Hollows said it was possible that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to "slow things down a bit" rather than defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hollows added, however, that the Reserve Bank would only act if it viewed the fall in the Kiwi as disorderly, something he said wasn't the case Friday.\par \par \uc2 While the focus was offshore, the New Zealand dollar was undermined also by news that dairy giant Fonterra had cut its forecast payout for the current season ending May 31 to NZ$6.00 per kilogram of milk solids from the NZ$6.60/kg it forecast just two months ago. Economists estimate the unscheduled cut will slice NZ$1 billion directly out of the economy.\par \par \uc2 Weak October credit card billings data, showing a 1.1% fall on month, was another reminder that consumer spending remains in the doldrums.\par \par \uc2 Traders said, however, that while the grim news added to the overall negative picture, the impact was relatively minor with the main driver being offshore markets.\par \par \uc2 "What happens in the local economy doesn't seem to matter too much at this stage," said Vrondas.\par \par \uc2 Government bonds yields and interest rate swaps also fell sharply, tracking offshore moves.\par \par \uc2 "Its been one-way traffic, following international moves and global sentiment," one local trader said.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the flow was light in New Zealand, with buyers thin on the ground. The news from Fonterra and the weak credit card billings had little impact given the global moves but added to the grim outlook and the pressure on yields.\par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; rebecca.howard@dowjones.com [ 21-11-08 0406GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1062 20711 4171   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081121e4bl00049\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
