\par\par \b \uc2 RBNZ sold a net NZ$14 million during November   \b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2007\par 01:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON, Dec 28 (Reuters) - The Reserve Bank of New Zealand (RBNZ) said on Friday it sold a net NZ$14 million ($10.8 million) of New Zealand dollars on the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during November.   \par \par \uc2  The figure compares with a net NZ$10 million sold in October.   \par \par \uc2  Back in June, the RBNZ sold a net NZ$736 million when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first time since the New Zealand dollar was floated 22 years ago to limit the rise in the kiwi.   \par \par \uc2  The figures are not a direct and complete indication of the amount spent on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and include liabilities of the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  government's Debt Management Office.   \par \par \uc2  The kiwi, which hit a post-float 22-year high of $0.8110 <NZD=D4> on July 24, fell sharply in August on risk aversion following the turmoil in global credit markets.   \par \par \uc2  It rebounded 7.5 percent in September and has since been volatile, with near-term direction swayed by movements in world equity markets.   \par \par \uc2  The kiwi was trading at around $0.7719/24 on Friday.   \par \par \uc2  Data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also showed its net short \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  position -- a figure which the RBNZ has said better reflects its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealings -- rose to NZ$2.48 billion from NZ$2.4 billion in October.   \par \par \uc2  A separate release by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed total household claims rose a seasonally adjusted 1.1 percent to NZ$166 billion in November, after gaining 0.8 percent in October. Borrowing was up 12.9 percent compared with November 2006.   \par \par \uc2  The full data is available on the Reserve Bank's Web site,   {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.rbnz.govt.nz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.rbnz.govt.nz  }}}\uc2   ($1=NZ$1.30)  (Reporting by Adrian Bathgate; Editing by James Thornhill)     \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-RBNZ/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ND|ABN|D|M|E|RBN|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071228e3cs0000r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
