\par\par \b \uc2 New Zealand cenbank sold net NZ$10 mln in October   \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2007\par 03:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON, Nov 29 (Reuters) - The Reserve Bank of New Zealand (RBNZ) said on Thursday it sold a net NZ$10 million ($7.8 million) of New Zealand dollars on the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during October.   \par \par \uc2 The figure compares with a net NZ$6 million bought in September.   \par \par \uc2  The RBNZ sold a net NZ$736 million in June when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first since the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was floated 22 years ago to limit the rise in the kiwi.   \par \par \uc2  The figures are not a direct and complete indication of the amount spent on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and include liabilities of the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  government's Debt Management Office.   \par \par \uc2  The kiwi, which hit a post-float 22-year high of $0.8110 <NZD=D4> on July 24, fell sharply in August on risk aversion following the turmoil in the global credit sector.   \par \par \uc2  It rebounded 7.5 percent in September and has since been volatile, with near-term direction swayed by movements in the global equity market.   \par \par \uc2  As of Thursday, the kiwi stood at around $0.7711/15.   \par \par \uc2  Data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also showed its net short \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  position -- a figure which the RBNZ has said better reflects its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealings -- rose to NZ$2.41 billion from NZ$2.4 billion in September.   \par \par \uc2  A separate release by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed total household claims rose a seasonally adjusted 0.8 percent to NZ$164.5 billion in October, after gaining at a similar pace in September. Borrowing was up 12.9 percent compared with October 2006.   \par \par \uc2  The full data is available on the Reserve Bank's website,   {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.rbnz.govt.nz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.rbnz.govt.nz  }}}\uc2      ($1=NZ$1.29)  (Reporting by Kazunori Takada)      \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-RBNZ/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ND|ABN|D|M|ABX|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071129e3bt0004q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
