\par\par \b \uc2 New Zealand's cenbank sold net NZ$1.5 bln in July   \b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2007\par 05:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, Aug 30 (Reuters) - The Reserve Bank of New Zealand (RBNZ) sold NZ$1.5 billion ($1.1 billion) of New Zealand dollars on a net basis on the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during July, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data released showed on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 The figure compares with a net NZ$736 million sold in June when the RBNZ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first since the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was floated 22 years ago to limit the rise in the kiwi.   \par \par \uc2 The figures are not a direct and complete indication of the amount spent on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and includes liabilities of the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  government's Debt Management Office.   \par \par \uc2 The data also showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's net short \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  position -- a figure which the RBNZ has said better reflected its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealings -- tripled to NZ$2.3 billion from NZ$702 million in June.   \par \par \uc2 The full data is available on the Reserve Bank of NZ's website,   {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.rbnz.govt.nz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.rbnz.govt.nz  }}}\par \par \uc2 The kiwi, which stood at around NZ$0.7720 at the beginning of July, rose to a post-float 22 year high of $0.8110 <NZD=D4> on July 24.   \par \par \uc2 However, it fell back to around $0.6650 by the end of the month after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signalled it did not expect to raise interest rates further and financial market volatility caused by credit sector woes.   \par \par \uc2 As of Thursday. the kiwi stood at $0.7045/51. ($1=NZ$1.41)   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-RBNZ/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT)|LANGEN|ND|ABN|D|M   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070902e38u0001e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
