\par\par \b \uc2 DJ RBNZ Sold Net NZ$2.26 Bln In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkt July Vs NZ$702M June   \b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2007\par 06:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2007, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The Reserve Bank of New Zealand sold a net 2.26 billion of New Zealand dollars in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in July, data issued Thursday by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed.   \par \par \uc2 A month earlier, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold a net NZ$702 million.   \par \par \uc2 The July figures don't provide complete data on the amount the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, as the numbers include liabilities of the New Zealand Debt Management Office.   \par \par \uc2 However, it indicates an escalation in its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after the unprecedented action June 11 to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. The June 11 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  attempted to knock back the high-flying local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the first such action since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in 1985. Since then, traders say, the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least on two more occasions in June, and thrice more in July.   \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ's attempt to clip the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's wings was only a partial success as the New Zealand dollar surged to a 25-year peak of US$0.8110 in late July before tumbling in recent weeks due to a shakeout in global markets caused by the U.S. subprime mortgage crisis.   \par \par \uc2 Thursday, the New Zealand dollar was trading at US$0.7048 at 0305 GMT, well below US$0.7600 levels at the end of July, on growing concerns over access to global credit. -By Shri Navaratnam, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; shri.navaratnam@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -0-    \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020070830e38u001md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
