\par\par \b \uc2 Reserve Bank Of NZ Sold Net NZ$702 Mln In June In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Market   \b0\par\par\uc2 249 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2007\par 06:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The Reserve Bank of New Zealand sold a net NZ$702 million of New Zealand dollars in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in June, data issued Monday by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed.   \par \par \uc2 A month earlier, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought a net NZ$58 million.   \par \par \uc2 The June figures don't provide complete data on the amount the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent in its unprecedented \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that month as the numbers include liabilities of the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Debt Management Office.   \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  June 11 to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar in an attempt to knock back the high-flying local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the first such action since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in 1985. Since then traders believe the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least on two more occasions in June, and twice more in July.   \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ's attempt to the clip the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's wings was only a partial success as the New Zealand dollar surged to a 25-year peak of US$0.8110 two weeks ago.   \par \par \uc2 The June \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently came when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was between US$0.7550 and US$0.7640.   \par \par \uc2 Monday, the New Zealand dollar was trading at US$0.7583, having come off sharply in the last several days on the back of growing concerns over global credit market woes.   \par \par \uc2 -By Shri Navaratnam, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; shri.navaratnam@dowjones.com [ 06-08-07 0444GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070806e3860004w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
