\par\par \b \uc2 NZ Govt Threat To Cool NZ Dlr May Damage RBNZ's Credibility   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Shri Navaratnam   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 1,029 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2007\par 07:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--Few believe Finance Minister Michael Cullen will override the New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's focus on inflation in a bid to stem the surging Kiwi dollar, but analysts say his recent comments on the subject undermine the credibility of the country's monetary policy framework.   \par \par \uc2 Persistently high underlying inflation has raised market expectations of another interest rate increase by the Reserve Bank of New Zealand at next week's policy meeting.   \par \par \uc2 But Cullen has rattled sections of the domestic market who worry that his remarks on the Policy Targets Agreement, or PTA, damages the standing of the RBNZ and its single-minded pursuit of monetary stability.   \par \par \uc2 "If the bank doesn't hike next week, and even if the reasons for (staying on hold) are the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's views on the economy, then people may wonder if there's been political interference," said  \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  chief economist Darren Gibbs.   \par \par \uc2 "So I think it's wholly unhelpful that these suggestions are being made or at least not being refuted by the finance minister," he added.   \par \par \uc2 While any action by the government to change the way interest rates are set by the RBNZ is likely to cause alarm bells in financial markets, it hasn't stopped Cullen from engaging lawmakers on the topic.   \par \par \uc2 Answering questions in Parliament over the last three days, the finance minister repeatedly referred to section 12 of the RBNZ Act, which gives the government the power to suspend the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inflation focus by amending the PTA.   \par \par \uc2 Under the PTA, the RBNZ sets monetary policy to keep annual inflation inside a 1%-3% band over the medium term.   \par \par \uc2 Cullen, who is also deputy prime minister, has refused to rule out the possibility of the government instructing the RBNZ to pursue a different objective. On Thursday, after being grilled by the opposition, the minister again warned speculators in the New Zealand dollar that section 12 could be invoked under the RBNZ Act.   \par \par \uc2 However, he stopped short of saying he would consider \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  under the act.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Herald newspaper quoted the minister as saying in its Thursday edition: "Section 12 is clearly there for a good reason. I would certainly not rule out its use."   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Stubborn Inflation Pressures Force Rates, NZ Dollar Up \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The country's high interest rates have lured offshore investors seeking high returns, with yen funded carry trades boosting the New Zealand dollar to record heights. Carry trades refer to borrowing in low interest rate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the yen to buy higher-yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  like the Kiwi dollar, and British pound.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stubborn domestic inflation pressures have forced RBNZ Governor Alan Bollard to raise interest rates in three quick moves this year, taking the Official Cash Rate to a record 8.00% - the highest policy rate in the developed world after Iceland.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 And nine of 15 economists surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires expect Bollard to tighten again at next week's rate-setting meeting, potentially giving another leg up to the New Zealand dollar, which tapped a fresh 25-year peak of US$0.7948 in overnight trade.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand dollar's strength has hobbled the country's export economy, prompting a storm of criticism against the government with opposition parties charging that the ruling Labour Party's high- spending ways of the past few years have complicated the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's fight against inflation.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some export businesses have also called for some form of action to kneecap the New Zealand dollar.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If section 12 is invoked, the government can direct the RBNZ to use monetary policy for a different economic objective for a 12-month period, and make this change public by negotiating a new interim PTA with the governor.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ANZ Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  chief economist Cameron Bagrie said that Cullen's comments on the PTA show "that there is considerable heat emerging over where the New Zealand dollar resides."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bagrie doesn't expect Cullen to alter the PTA but said the minister's view underscores the fact that the government has ultimate authority over the functions of the RBNZ.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "While the Reserve Bank has independence, it is merely \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  independence, and its continuation resides with the discretion of the government," he added.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's inflation eased to 2% on year in the second quarter, inside the RBNZ's target band, but domestic inflation - which excludes import prices - remains at an uncomfortable 4.1%.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ruling Labour Trail Opposition In Polls   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The anti-New Zealand dollar rhetoric by Cullen may partly reflect the Labour Party-led coalition's poor showing in polls,  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Gibbs said. With an election due late in 2008, the main opposition National Party has galloped ahead of Labour in recent polls.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While politically it may make sense for the Labour Party to be seen as taking action against the high local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Gibbs thinks the finance minister's comments were mere "bluster."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It would be an extremely stupid move (changing the objective of PTA) and I don't see him doing it," he said. The powers of section 12 in the RBNZ Act were intended for use only during a major economic upheaval or crisis, Gibbs added.   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders say the New Zealand dollar is likely to head north of US$0.8000 over the short-term due to a broadly weaker U.S. dollar, and rising domestic interest rates.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 They note that the unprecedented \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market by the RBNZ on June 11 - the first such action since the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was floated in 1985 - had failed to knock back the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We continue to view the persistent verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the NZ government and actual \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the RBNZ as opportunities to buy NZD/USD on dips," said Sue Trinh, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at  \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBC Capital Markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand dollar was trading at US$0.7917 at 0457 GMT, off an intraday peak of US$0.7938   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -Shri Navaratnam, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; shri.navaratnam@dowjones.com    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Karen Lane [ 19-07-0