\par\par \b \uc2 NZ Dlr Ends Up, But May Correct Lower On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears   \b0\par\par\uc2 472 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2007\par 07:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                           Close        Change \par  NZD/USD                  0.7824       +0.0017 \par  NZD/AUD                  0.9029       -0.0030 \par  July 2009 Bond           7.610%       +10.5 bps \par  Dec 2017 Bond            6.820%       +6.0 bps \par  10-Year U.S. Spread      +169.0 bps   +1.0 bps \par  90-Day Bank Bill         8.41%        +6.0 bps \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The New Zealand dollar closed higher Friday but well off its session highs, as investors were spooked by the news that the Reserve Bank of New Zealand plans to hold some of its foreign reserves on an unhedged basis in the future, to better defend against any sharp moves in the value of the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Mike Hollows, director of trading at Auckland-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  concern HIFX, said the change to a more open position on foreign reserves was "reasonably significant" as it effectively doubles the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's firepower to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sell down the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "RBNZ are clearly very, very serious (about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) if they're prepared to change the way they manage their reserves. The fact they've got potentially double their fire power is quite a focusing thing for those that are sitting long New Zealand dollars right now," Hollows said.   \par \par \uc2 He thinks the news may provide a "good excuse" for a corrective move lower for the Kiwi near term, after the unit failed a test of technical resistance around US$0.7880 on the back of stronger-than-expected retail sales data for May earlier in the session.   \par \par \uc2 Hollows pegged support at US$0.7790 and resistance at US$0.7880 overnight.   \par \par \uc2 Still, others were wary about reading too much into the RBNZ statement.   \par \par \uc2 "This statement has no implications for rate decisions or the timing of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said ABN Amro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Greg Gibbs, who noted the bank hadn't changed its criteria for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Earlier, data showed retail sales rose 1.2% in May from April, above market expectations for a 0.5% rise, potentially raising the chance the RBNZ could hike interest rates again at its July 26 meeting, economists said.   \par \par \uc2 However, second quarter consumer inflation data due Monday remains the key decider for the bank's policy stance, they said.   \par \par \uc2 Government bonds ended lower as a sell off in shorter dated bonds due to an "overhang of supply" weighed across the curve, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 The selloff was exacerbated by the retail sales data, which surprised the market and "puts a July hike back on the radar screen," said one local trader.   \par \par \uc2 Market pricing moved to above a 40% chance of a hike in July from 24% prior to the data.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rachel Pannett, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; rachel.pannett@dowjones.com [ 13-07-07 0537GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1062 20711 4171   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070713e37d0004w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
