\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-NZ retail sales jump in May, kiwi rises   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kazunori Takada   \par \uc2 591 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2007\par 01:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst's comment, updates market reaction)   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, July 13 (Reuters) - New Zealand retail sales surged in May, data showed on Friday, reinforcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hawkish anti-inflation policy and sending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to within a whisker of a 22-year post float high.   \par \par \uc2 Seasonally adjusted sales rose 1.2 percent in May, driven by higher car and supermarket sales, following a 1.2 percent fall in April. Economists in a Reuters poll had forecast sales to gain 0.4 percent on the previous month.   \par \par \uc2 "It keeps things boiling along, so there's still a tangible risk of another rate hike later this month," said  \uc2 UBS\uc2  senior economist Robin Clements.   \par \par \uc2 All eyes would be on second-quarter inflation data, due on Monday, which could be the catalyst for the Reserve Bank of New Zealand to lift interest rates to 8.25 percent at its next review on July 26, analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar <NZD=> surged on the sales data to gain more than a quarter of a cent to around NZ$0.7879, just shy of a 22-year post float high of $0.7881 reached earlier in the month. Bank bills were sold off, with the yield on the September contract <NBBU7> rising six basis points to 8.44 percent.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand has raised its official cash rate by a total of 75 basis points this year to 8 percent on concerns over strong domestic spending, robust housing market and rising payouts to dairy farmers.   \par \par \uc2 RBNZ Governor Alan Bollard told Reuters in an interview in June that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not ease monetary policy until it sees a clear slowdown in consumer demand and house price inflation.   \par \par \uc2 Rising interest rates have been the main driver behind the rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to moderate the pace of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.   \par \par \uc2 FOCUS ON INFLATION DATA   \par \par \uc2 Statistics New Zealand said May retail sales were driven higher by rises in motor vehicle and supermarket retailing, which gained 4.4 percent and 1.9 percent respectively.   \par \par \uc2 Core sales, which exclude car and fuel sales, rose 0.8 percent in May, following a 0.9 percent fall in the previous month and compared with a forecast for 0.3 percent rise.   \par \par \uc2 On a year ago, actual sales also rose a more-than-expected 6.7 percent.   \par \par \uc2 The market currently sees about a 45 percent chance of a another rate hike later in the month, up sharply from around 23 percent on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the Monday's consumer price index, which is forecast to show a rise of 0.8 percent on the previous quarter, would be deciding factor for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ forecast in June the CPI to rise 0.7 percent in the second quarter, up from 0.5 percent gain the March quarter.   \par \par \uc2 "All eyes are on Monday's CPI and that will determine whether they go or not in July," said Khoon Goh, senior economist at ANZ-National Bank.   \par \par \uc2 Fourteen of 17 analysts in the latest Reuters poll expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep rates on hold at its next review on July 26.   \par \par \uc2 Latest data from government agency Quotable Value showed the annual pace of house value growth accelerated for the fifth straight month in June, rising 12.2 percent from a year earlier.   \par \par \uc2 NEWZEALAND ECONOMY/RETAIL (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ND|ABN|D|M|ABX|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070712e37c00001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
