\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS- \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  may let C$, not rates, cool growth   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Louise Egan   \par \uc2 736 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2007\par 20:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 OTTAWA, July 10 (Reuters) - The  \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  is unlikely to implement a long series of interest rate hikes following its rate rise on Tuesday, and is seen relying instead on the soaring Canadian dollar to cool economic growth and inflation.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  came off the sidelines on Tuesday after holding rates steady for more than a year, and lifted its key overnight lending target by one-quarter point to 4.50 percent. It said "some modest further increase" in the rate may be needed.   \par \par \uc2 But reading between the lines in its statement there was a dovish undertone to the hawkish headline, leaving analysts with the clear impression the bank is not quite ready to commit to more than one more rate increase in the near term.   \par \par \uc2 "The stronger Canadian dollar is putting a little bit of a damper on the extent of the tightening that might be required, and that is what the bank is basically telling people," said Marc Levesque, chief market strategist at TD Securities.   \par \par \uc2 After the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made its rate announcement on Tuesday, the Canadian dollar dropped as low as C$1.0542 to the U.S. dollar, or 94.86 U.S. cents, from C$1.0496, or 95.27 U.S. cents, at Monday's close. At midafternoon on Tuesday it was at C$1.0516, or 95.09 U.S. cents.   \par \par \uc2 The bank revealed nothing of its analysis of the reasons for the Canadian dollar's meteoric rise to 30-year highs in recent weeks. It did say, however, that the higher trading range for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , combined with higher interest rates across the yield curve, would dull economic growth in 2008 and 2009. The higher Canadian dollar could keep the inflation rate below the bank's estimate, it also said.   \par \par \uc2 "Those things suggest they're going to be keeping their eye closely on the Canadian dollar, see how it performs between now and September before they make a decision as to what they're going to do in September," said Ted Carmichael of  \uc2 J.P. Morgan Canada.\par \par \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  and TD Securities both expect just one more rate hike on Sept. 5 followed by another pause.   \par \par \uc2 Bank Governor David Dodge said last month that the gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since April had been faster than past experience would suggest but he was unclear on whether that would influence interest rates.   \par \par \uc2 While the bank has no target for the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, it does react to any sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements that are out of line with economic pressures. Some economists say the recent gains have been of the undesirable variety, or so-called Type 2 -- fueled by market expectations of a rate hike, rather than by strong demand for commodities.   \par \par \uc2 "Citing the strong loonie as a key downside risk is a new development and is a mild hint that the bank views some of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gain as Type 2," said Doug Porter, deputy chief economist at BMO Capital Markets, in a research note.   \par \par \uc2 Stewart Hall, market strategist at  \uc2 HSBC\uc2 , suggests that the  \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  was deliberately vague on the details of future rate hikes to put the brakes on the Canadian dollar. "The breadth and timing of the cycle is uncertain, and it is this uncertainty that will spare the  \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  from the challenges currently confronting the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in the market to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last several weeks   \par \par \uc2 Several economists noted that the bank's use of the word "modest" when referring to further rate hikes has been used in the past to signal just one more hike in a cycle.   \par \par \uc2 But the bank also has to fend off pesky inflation pressures that will not go away. Economists expect core inflation to climb to nearly 3 percent later this year as the effects of a June 2006 sales tax cut will no longer have the effect of reducing the 12-month figures.   \par \par \uc2 "It would be very difficult for the bank to see an inflation rate that's that much above their 2 percent target and not do at least one more rate hike," Carmichael said.   \par \par \uc2 CANADA-BANK/RATES-DOLLAR (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|M|D|CANT   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070713e37a001r6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
