\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-RBNZ says  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  aims to moderate peaks   \b0\par\par\uc2 543 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2007\par 05:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst comment, prices, details)   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed at moderating the rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar and not to defend a certain \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  level.   \par \par \uc2 In an article written for media, Reserve Bank of New Zealand Deputy Governor Grant Spencer said the strong kiwi dollar was hurting the country's exporters and current levels could not be sustained given the country's large current account deficit.   \par \par \uc2 "It does not attempt to defend a particular level of the exchange rate. Rather it sends a signal that, in the bank's view, the exchange rate is out of alignment with the economic fundamentals," Spencer said.   \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar three times since June 11, when it stepped in for the first time since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in 1985.   \par \par \uc2 Spencer said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was an ongoing process and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not confirm specific activities. The RBNZ confirmed its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but has not commented on its subsequent forays.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar showed little reaction to Spencer's comments, trading around $0.7645 <NZD=>, about half a U.S. cent below a 22-year post-float high of $0.7695 hit the previous day.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said there was nothing surprising in the article and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  when trading volumes were most light to maximise the impact.   \par \par \uc2 "What they are going to do now is be selective in terms of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and probably try to time it when they can get bigger impact for their buck." said ANZ-National Bank senior economist Khoon Goh.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has risen around 10 percent since March, lifted by demand for carry trades, where investors raise money in low yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to invest in high yielding ones.   \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Japanese Finance Minister Koji Omi warned investors to be wary of the risks of one-way bets against the yen, in an apparent reference to carry trades.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials from South Korea and New Zealand also expressed concern over the yen's weakness at a meeting in Seoul, and agreed a potential unwinding of yen carry trades was a big threat to financial markets.   \par \par \uc2 They also agreed that potentially-affected countries needed to deal with the issue in a pre-emptive manner.   \par \par \uc2 Spencer reiterated that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not signal a change in the direction of monetary policy, which was dependent on how inflation pressures evolve over the months ahead.   \par \par \uc2 "Evidence that inflation pressures are abating will be an important step in seeing the exchange rate return to more sustainable levels," he added.   \par \par \uc2 On June 7, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unexpectedly raised interest rates to 8 percent -- the highest in the industrialised world -- because of concerns over the strength in consumer spending and a rampant housing market.   \par \par \uc2 Fourteen of 16 economists in a Reuters poll expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep policy on hold at its next review on July 26. (The full text of the RBNZ article can be viewed by clicking on [ID:nWEL184455].)   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-RBNZ/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ND|ABN|D|E|RBN|M|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070627e36r0004g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
