\par\par \b \uc2 NZ dlr nudges up towards 22-yr highs, bonds flat   \b0\par\par\uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 2007\par 23:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 26 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar <NZD=> nudged up towards 22-year post-float highs as traders awaited a slew of key data due later in the week.   \par \par \uc2 * Kiwi traded $0.7643-$0.7667 in local trade, within sight    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the high of $0.7687 -- its strongest since the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was\par floated in 1985 -- hit on Monday.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Data showed New Zealand electronic retail cards spending rose just 0.1 percent in May following interest rate rises earlier in the year aimed at curbing consumer spending. It rose 1 percent in April.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Traders focused on first quarter growth data and National Bank's business outlook survey due on Friday. Economists expect Q1 growth to pick up to 1 percent from 0.8 percent in Q4.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Before that, May trade figures and Q2 consumer confidence report will be released on Wednesday and Q1 current account and May building numbers on Thursday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * More \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  expected if the kiwi continues to push higher. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped in again in late U.S. trade on Friday although the impact was short-lived.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * NZ bonds unchanged after U.S. Treasuries gained on weak performance on Wall Street. A tender of 98-day T-bills produced successful weighted average yield of 7.838 percent.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------June 26 snapshot at 3.20 p.m. (0320\par GMT)------------