\par\par \b \uc2 NZ dollar trades tight range on Japanese buying   \b0\par\par\uc2 426 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2007\par 23:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 22 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar <NZD=> held a tight range around $0.7630 on Friday as a steady stream of buying from Japanese investors seeking high yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  underpinned the kiwi.   \par \par \uc2 There was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite the kiwi hitting a post-float high of $0.7660 in Asian trade on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 "There's more demand coming out of Japan, which is not just going into kiwi," Westpac \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Michael Gordon said.   \par \par \uc2 The kiwi has been a beneficiary of the carry trade -- where investors borrow a low yielder such as the yen to invest in the high yielding kiwi. New Zealand interest rates are 8 percent, the highest in the industrialised world.   \par \par \uc2 The Australian and New Zealand dollars have long been favourites of Japanese investors and are used for carry trades.   \par \par \uc2 A trader at a Japanese trust bank said he saw constant flows from investment trusts buying the euro and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of emerging markets that have become popular recently.   \par \par \uc2 The yen hit a 20-year low against the kiwi, a four and a half year low against the U.S. dollar and a 16-year low against the Australian dollar.   \par \par \uc2 At 0500 GMT the kiwi was at $0.7637/47, up from $0.7626/29 in late local trade on Wednesday, having traded a $0.7629 to $0.7645 range. It hit a high of 94.71 against the yen <NZDJPY=R>.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has twice \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past two weeks to lower the kiwi, but traders say the bank is wary of trying to take on the market by defending a set level.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have come on the past two Mondays, when closure in offshore markets meant maximum impact, but market-watchers say \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the third Monday in a row would be too predictable.   \par \par \uc2 The NZ dollar trade weighted index (TWI) <=NZD>, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's preferred \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  measure, was at 74.40, after hitting a record high of 74.62 on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 New Zealand credit card billing rose a seasonally adjusted 0.5 percent in May, compared with the previous months 0.9 percent fall.   \par \par \uc2 Next week sees a host of important data, including gross domestic product, trade and current account figures.   \par \par \uc2 New Zealand bonds firmed, as U.S. Treasuries held steady, with yields falling two basis points.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-NEWZEALAND-DOLLAR (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|ND|ABX|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070624e36l000ij\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
