\par\par \b \uc2 NZ dollar quiet near 22-year highs, no sign of RBNZ   \b0\par\par\uc2 492 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2007\par 23:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 22 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar <NZD=> stayed in a tight range but close to its 22-year post float high on Friday, as investors chasing its yield shrugged off any threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 * Kiwi spent most of the local session in a $0.7630-0.7640 range after hitting a post-float high of $0.7660 in Asian trading on Thursday. NZ dollar trade weighted index <=NZD> was also just below its new post-float high of 74.62.   \par \par \uc2 * No sign that Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  is looking to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again, despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  being above the levels at which it entered the market previously. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to be wary about being seen to go against market trend or trying to defend a level in the kiwi or the trade weighted index <=NZD>. However, the threat of more hit and run selling by the RBNZ is keeping investors wary.   \par \par \uc2 * Yen falls to a 4-\u189\'00\'BD year year low against the U.S. dollar <JPY=> as investors use it to finance their investment in high yielding assets, such as kiwi and Aussie dollars.   \par \par \uc2 * Kiwi touching 20-year high against the yen <NZDJPY=R> as new Japanese investment trusts being launched were reportedly seeking as much as $3 billion. Aussie dollar and sterling also at multi-year highs against the yen.   \par \par \uc2 * NZ credit card billings rose seasonally adjusted 0.5 percent in May compared with the previous month's 0.9 percent fall. Next week sees a slew of data, including trade, current account and gross domestic product.   \par \par \uc2 * NZ bonds recover opening weakness to be flat on the day as long-dated U.S. Treasuries weaken on a flood of new corporate issuance, although short-dated maturities steady on    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par safe haven trade. -------------June 22 snapshot at 4.00 p.m.\par (0400 GMT)------------\par            (figures in brackets are from June 21) 90-DAY\par BILLS (SEP)  91.60 (PREV 91.60)   90-DAYS 8.36 (PREV 8.36)\par 90-DAY BILLS (DEC)  91.59 (PREV 91.60)   07/08   7.46 (PREV\par 7.46) 90-DAY BILLS (MAR)  91.62 (PREV 91.61)   11/11   7.16\par (PREV 7.16) NZD TRADE WEIGHTED  74.40 (PREV 74.28)   04/13  \par 7.07 (PREV 7.07) NZD/USD   0.7630/40   (PREV 0.7619/29)   12/17\par   6.78 (PREV 6.78) NZD/AUD   0.9014/26   (PREV 0.9021/32)  RBNZ\par MCI+1461 (PREV+1453) NZD/EUR   0.5697/06   (PREV 0.5688/00)  US\par 10-YR 5.19 (PREV 5.14) NZD/JPY    94.50/63   (PREV  93.14/31) \par AU 10-YR 6.26 (PREV 6.29) ***SPREADS: NZ/US 10-YR +159 (+164)  \par   NZ/AUS 10-YR +52 (+49)***\par ----------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-NEWZEALAND-DOLLAR (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|ND|ABX|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070624e36l000ii\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
