\par\par \b \uc2 NZ dollar strikes 22-year high vs US dollar   \b0\par\par\uc2 185 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2007\par 08:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, June 21 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar punched to a 22-year high against the U.S. dollar on Thursday as investors chased its steep yield and shrugged off the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength in the past two weeks.   \par \par \uc2 The kiwi jumped to a high of $0.7660 <NZD=D4> on the Reuters dealing system, up 0.8 percent, with traders saying the market wanted to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's willingness to limit its rise.   \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar was also up nearly 1 percent to a 20-year high near 94.70 yen <NZDJPY=R> as market players used the low-yielding Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a cheap source of funds to buy higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 New Zealand's short-term rates are the highest in the industrialised world at 8 percent, while Japan's are the lowest at 0.5 percent.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -NZDOLLAR (URGENT)|LANGEN|NAT|ABN|D|J|M|Z|E|RBN|SI|AUF|ND|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070621e36l000cu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
