\par\par \b \uc2 NZ dollar holds near 22-year high, bond yields rise   \b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2007\par 22:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 19 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar <NZD=> held near its 22-year post-float high on Thursday as the market looked to whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to lower the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Ongoing yield buying meant a fresh high for the soaring kiwi was only a matter of time, said Sue Trinh, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \uc2 RBC Capital Markets.\par \par \uc2 "The overall appetite for yield remains very strong," Trinh said.   \par \par \uc2 At 0500 GMT the kiwi was at $0.7626/29, having hit a high of $0.7635, up from $0.7588/98 in late local trading on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has twice \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past 11 days to lower the kiwi, and Trinh said it is likely to move again soon.   \par \par \uc2 "The market looks increasingly willing to test the RBNZ's resolve in regards to its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Trinh said.   \par \par \uc2 The kiwi has been a beneficiary of the carry trade, where investors borrow a low yielder such as the yen to invest in a high yielder.   \par \par \uc2 That demand saw the yen hit a 20-year low against the kiwi, and a four and a half year low against the U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The NZ dollar trade weighted index (TWI) <=NZD>, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's preferred \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  measure, was at 74.34, retreating from a session high of 74.41, but approaching the life-time high of 74.54 reached in December 2005.   \par \par \uc2 Next week's first quarter gross domestic product reading is the next significant piece of data.   \par \par \uc2 New Zealand bonds were weaker as U.S. Treasuries fell, ending a three-day rally on weaker European bond prices, with yields rising two to three basis points.   \par \par \uc2 A government bond tender for NZ$200 million in bonds met firm demand from the market. The government offered NZ$100 million in July 2009 bonds and NZ$50 million each of November 2011 and April 2015 paper.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-NEWZEALAND-DOLLAR (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|ND|ABX|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070623e36k000ja\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
