\par\par \b \uc2 NZ dollar hovers near $0.76, RBNZ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  eyed   \b0\par\par\uc2 570 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2007\par 23:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 19 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar <NZD=> held near nine-day highs on Wednesday, as wary investors looked for any sign that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be ready for another bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The kiwi spent much of the session just below $0.7600, a level regarded by some as likely to set off alarm bells at the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  and possibly trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "In light of the recent RBNZ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market participants are still reluctant to chase the NZD higher," said Bank of New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Danica Hampton.   \par \par \uc2 At 0500 GMT the kiwi was at $0.7588/98 from $0.7552/55 in late local trading on Tuesday. It briefly touched a local session high of $0.7600 but traded no lower $0.7577.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on June 11 for the first time since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated 22 years ago and was seen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market again last Monday.   \par \par \uc2 The first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  sent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 2 percent lower from a high of $0.7640, while the second foray at around $0.7550 sent the kiwi half a cent lower.   \par \par \uc2 The kiwi followed trends in the broader market, where the U.S dollar slipped after a pull back in bond yields which had been boosting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the yen was at multi-year lows on increased carry trades to take advantage of its low yield.   \par \par \uc2 The kiwi has been a beneficiary of the carry trade, where investors borrow a low yielder such as the yen to invest in a high yielder.   \par \par \uc2 "While there has been a steady stream of Japanese retail demand, leverage and momentum funds out of Asia have also been noted buyers," Hampton said.   \par \par \uc2 Investors were also watching the NZ dollar trade weighted index (TWI) <=NZD>, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's preferred \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  measure. On that basis 74, is seen as a possible trigger point for the RBNZ.   \par \par \uc2 The NZ dollar TWI was at 73.90, up 0.4 percent on the day. The index's life-time high is 74.54 reached in December 2005.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unmoved by data showing a net seasonally adjusted gain of 360 long term and permanent migrants in May, nearly double the gain in April. The annual gain of 10,680 was up 4 percent on a year ago.   \par \par \uc2 Immigration gains were running at about half the RBNZ's forecast rate, which would help reduce domestic demand.   \par \par \uc2 "The easing in net migration may give the Reserve Bank some comfort on the housing front although the raft of key housing data remains far too strong," said  \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  senior economist Su-Lin Ong, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could afford to watch and wait.   \par \par \uc2 A warning by Finance Minister Michael Cullen that the property market might undergo a sharp correction also passed without effect.   \par \par \uc2 Next week's first quarter gross domestic product reading is the significant piece of data.   \par \par \uc2 New Zealand bonds were firmer as U.S. Treasuries drifted sideways after a three-day rally as weak housing data reinforced the view that U.S. interest rates will stay on hold.   \par \par \uc2 The yield on benchmark NZ December 2017 bond <NZG1217=RNZL> closed three basis points lower at 6.76 percent.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-NEWZEALAND-DOLLAR (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|ND|ABX|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070622e36j0021a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
