\par\par \b \uc2 NZ dollar hits $0.76, retreats on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears   \b0\par\par\uc2 423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2007\par 23:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 20 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar <NZD=> hit a nine-day high of $0.76 on choppy trade, helped by yield-demand and Australian dollar strength.   \par \par \uc2 * Kiwi keeps a tight $0.7577 to $0.76 range, helped by increasing risk appetite among investors as stock markets rebound from recent sell-offs.   \par \par \uc2 * Kiwi at 0350 GMT at 0.7585/95. Many traders see $0.76 as a natural cap, at which market fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower. It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in over two decades on June 11 when the kiwi was around $0.7630.   \par \par \uc2 * Support for the kiwi seen from $0.7555.   \par \par \uc2 * Aussie dollar <AUD=> near an 18-year high against the U.S. dollar, and a 16-year peak against the yen, as investors chase high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 * Migration gains increased in May, official data showed, with a net gain of 10,680 permanent migrants for the year to May, compared with 10,190 for the May 2006 year.   \par \par \uc2 * Finance Minister Michael Cullen told a parliamentary committee the housing market was at risk of a downturn, which would leave some homeowners exposed to financial hardship.   \par \par \uc2 * NZ bonds firmed, with yields slipping two basis points along the curve, as U.S. Treasuries rose for the third day in a row on fears the housing sector would be a drag on the economy.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------June 20 snapshot at 3.40 p.m. (0340\par GMT)------------\par            (figure