\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-NZ dollar seen near peak, to ease in 2008   \b0\par\par\uc2 631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2007\par 07:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 19 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar <NZD=> is seen peaking in the next few months before gradually easing in 2008 as domestic spending softens and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  looks to start easing its tight monetary policy, a Reuters poll showed on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to stem the rise in the kiwi dollar after two such moves in the past week, but analysts say it was unlikely to have a significant impact on the market.   \par \par \uc2 "We expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will peak in the next two or three month but I don't think (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) will necessarily be the driver that pushes it back," said Danica Hampton, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one of those things that affect sentiment rather than materially impacting the real economy."   \par \par \uc2 The Reuters poll of 10 analysts has a median forecast for the kiwi of US$0.73 at the end of September and $0.72 at the end of December, before it is seen easing to $0.6720 by the end of June next year.   \par \par \uc2 As of Tuesday, the New Zealand dollar was trading at $0.7545/55, about one U.S. cent the below a 22-year post float high struck on June 8 after the RBNZ unexpectedly raised interest rates to 8 percent.   \par \par \uc2 In the previous poll taken before the June rate review, analysts expected the kiwi to stand at $0.73 at the end of September and $0.65 in June next year.   \par \par \uc2 On the RBNZ's preferred trade-weighted basis <=NZD>, the New Zealand dollar is seen at 71.4 at the end of September, easing to 70.6 and 66.6 in December and June, respectively. The RBNZ forecast the trade-weighted index to average 72 in the second half of 2007 and 71.6 in the first half of 2008.   \par \par \uc2 On June 11, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in 1985, and sold what it said was an exceptionally and unjustifiably high kiwi dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Market sources said the RBNZ stepped in again on Monday, although on a smaller scale, which briefly pushed the New Zealand dollar down about half a U.S. cent.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the long-term direction would be set by the strength in the economy and interest rates.   \par \par \uc2 Bank of New Zealand's Hampton said she expected to see the New Zealand dollar ease towards the end of the year, but it could hold up longer if consumer spending does not cool.   \par \par \uc2 The poll also showed 13 of 16 forecasters do not expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise interest again, after lifting them for the third straight time on June 7 [nWEL270282].    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  -    NEW ZEALAND DOLLAR, AT SEPT 30, 2007 (10 RESPONDENTS)\par  Previous median in brackets (June 5)\par                           Median       Average      Range\par  NZD TWI                   71.0 (70.4)     70.8     67.4 to\par 64.0\par  NZD/USD (cents)           73.0 (73.0)     73.4     70.0 to\par 77.4\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \par  NEW ZEALAND DOLLAR, AT DEC 31, 2007 (10 RESPONDENTS)\par                           Median       Average      Range\par  NZD TWI                      69.1         68.4     63.1 to\par 74.2\par  NZD/USD (cents)              72.0         70.9     65.0 to\par 75.1\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \par  NEW ZEALAND DOLLAR, AT JUNE 30, 2008 (10 RESPONDENTS)\par  Previous median in brackets (June 5)\par                           Median       Average      Range\par  NZD TWI                   64.8 (63.1)     65.6     62.7 to\par 71.0\par  NZD/USD (cents)           67.2 (65.0)     66.9     63.0 to\par 71.0\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Respondents to the poll: ANZ-National Bank, ASB Bank, Bank of NZ,  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2 ,  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 ,  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs JBWere\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Infometrics, Macquarie,  \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  NZ, Westpac.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 NEWZEALAND-ECONOMY/POLL-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|Table|ND|ABN|D|M|E|RBN|ABX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070622e36j0008w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
