\par\par \b \uc2 3rd UPDATE: RBNZ Apparent Action To Sell NZD Under Fire   \b0\par\par\uc2 954 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2007\par 07:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds closing levels for NZ dollar and bonds as well as analysts' comments.)   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     By Shri Navaratnam \par     Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second time in a week appears to have had little lasting impact, although the threat of further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action looms.   \par \par \uc2 Some analysts say the RBNZ is fighting a losing battle.   \par \par \uc2 Earlier Monday a government official, who spoke on condition of anonymity, told Dow Jones Newswires that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold the Kiwi to cap any momentum in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  toward 76 U.S. cents.   \par \par \uc2 "I can confirm that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  this morning - it was modest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if you like - the (RBNZ) wants to hurt any rallies toward 76 (U.S.) cents," the official said.   \par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman declined to say whether the RBNZ had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, but dealers said it had.   \par \par \uc2 "They (RBNZ) were in the market earlier (Monday), offering around the 75.50 (U.S.) cent level," said Danica Hampton, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of New Zealand said.   \par \par \uc2 Hampton said that according to market talk, the RBNZ may have sold up to NZ$350 million. However, the reported local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling appears to have lost its impact beyond the initial selloff.   \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar slipped to a low of US$0.7504 from as high as US$0.7554 this morning, but had recovered most of its losses and closed the domestic session at US$0.7547 at 0500 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 The reported selling of the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar comes after last week's unprecedented \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the first since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in March 1985.   \par \par \uc2 "Financial markets, particularly \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, are far bigger than any one player," said Clifford Bennett, chief economist at FxMax. "The RBNZ is a relatively small bank, and its attempt to cap the New Zealand dollar bull trend is a mistake. "The carry trade will continue to dominate, and it is the RBNZ's own policy that has made them a carry trade target," Bennett said.   \par \par \uc2 "Expect their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , waves of selling to have decreasing effect, until finally the market runs dramatically higher," he said.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     RBNZ Says Kiwi Unjustifiably High \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Following last week's RBNZ action, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers and analysts have said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is likely to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again if the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which hit a post-float high of US$0.7640 earlier this month, continues to rise.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The RBNZ last week said it sold the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  because the Kiwi had reached an exceptionally high level that wasn't justified by economic fundamentals.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The pair had since been trapped in an 80-point range, trading between US$0.7460 to US$0.7540 as traders were reluctant to push the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  too high.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, with the Bank of Japan leaving interest rates unchanged Friday, renewed demand for carry trades saw the New Zealand dollar pushed higher over the weekend.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's benchmark policy rate of 8.00% - the highest in the developed world after Iceland - has attracted inflows from carry trades, where investors borrow in low-yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to invest in higher-yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The RBNZ has said it will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is unjustifiably high and when the conditions are right. According to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , when carried out, would also have to meet its policy target agreement.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The agreement obliges the RBNZ to maintain price stability while avoiding unnecessary volatility in output, interest rates and the exchange rate.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The government source said the RBNZ isn't eyeing specific levels to determine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  but it wants to knock back any renewed upward momentum in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There is no set policy on this (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ), but they seem to be very uncomfortable with any indication the market may resume the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rally," he said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The source said that at this stage the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appears to be more comfortable with the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading close to US$0.7500.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An  \f28 \uc2 \f2 ANZ Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  dealer said it will be "very difficult" for the RBNZ to fight global trends toward higher-yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . As long as New Zealand interest rates remain attractive, the Kiwi will continue to encourage speculative investors, he said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week said its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't prejudice the future direction of monetary policy.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RBNZ Governor Alan Bollard surprised markets earlier this month by raising the Official Cash Rate by a quarter percentage point to a record high to knock back resilient domestic demand pressures.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It was the third consecutive rate increase this year, and economists say the risks of another tightening remain high due to broadly solid data and continuing inflationary pressures.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There was muted reaction in the debt markets Monday to the reported RBNZ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Bond prices rose but underperformed their U.S. counterparts as the market continues to price in about a 50% chance of another rate hike in New Zealand by September.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bond prices are expected to remain trapped in a range, with bias to sell on rallies. The New Zealand dollar should probably stay capped below US$0.7600, dealers said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                           Close        Change \par  NZD/USD                  0.7547       +0.0027 \par  NZD/AUD                  0.8960       -0.0022 \par  July 2009 Bond           7.300%       -3.0 bps \par  December 2017 Bond       6.805%       +3.5 bps \par  10-Year U.S. Spread      +155.0 bps   -4.5 bps \par  90-Day Bank Bill         8.33%        -1.0 bp \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Shri Navaratnam, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; shri.navaratnam@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Mary de Wet [ 18-06-07 0537GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 1062 20711 4171   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070618e36i0005q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
