\par\par \b \uc2 New Zealand stocks up 2 pct, merger talk helps   \b0\par\par\uc2 251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2007\par 03:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON, June 18 (Reuters) - New Zealand stocks rose over 2 percent on Monday as takeover talk surrounding the country's biggest airport and reported \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped the market reverse two weeks of declines.   \par \par \uc2  The benchmark NZX-50 index <.NZ50> was up 77 points or 1.8 percent at 4,289.59 at 0135 GMT, having traded as high as 4,303.405.   \par \par \uc2  "Absolutely, it's been spurred by Auckland Airport's rise," said ABN AMRO Craigs head of equities, Bryon Burke.   \par \par \uc2 Auckland International Airport Ltd\uc2  , a top-10 stock with a 6.3 percent weighting in the index, vaulted 17 percent after it said it was talking to investors who might take a stake in it.   \par \par \uc2  Some of its shareholders had turned down a NZ$3.10 a share offer from a Canadian pension fund [ID:nWEL717404]. AIA last traded up 11.7 percent at NZ$3.15.   \par \par \uc2  The news ignited other leading stocks, with all top-10 stocks, which account for around two-thirds of the market, gaining.   \par \par \uc2  "The sell-side of most stocks has been very thin and so any buying has pushed most stocks up," Burke said.   \par \par \uc2  Reports the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap a rise in the NZ dollar, a possible pointer to the end of interest rate rises, were also positive for stocks.  ($1=NZ$1.33)      \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-NEWZEALAND-STOCKS|LANGEN|AUF|ND|ABN|E|RBN|ABX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070618e36i0002h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
