\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: RBNZ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  To Sell NZ Dlr For 2nd Time In A Wk   \b0\par\par\uc2 387 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2007\par 00:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail)   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second time in a week Monday.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't confirm it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, but dealers said the bank was in the market selling the New Zealand dollar. The action from the RBNZ comes after last week's unprecedented \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the first since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in 1985.   \par \par \uc2 "They (RBNZ) were in the market earlier, offering around the 75.50 (US) cent level," said Danica Hampton, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of New Zealand said.   \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar has eased off to US$0.7523 from as high as US$0.7560 earlier this morning.   \par \par \uc2 Another dealer at HSBC said the RBNZ was seen offering in the high 75 U.S. cent area.   \par \par \uc2 He said the RBNZ appears determined to lean against any sustained uptrend in the Kiwi. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers have said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which hit a post-float high of US$0.7640 earlier this month, continued to rise.   \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ last week said it sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the Kiwi was exceptionally high and was unjustified by economic fundamentals.   \par \par \uc2 The pair had since been trapped in a 80 point range, trading between US$0.7460 to US$0.7540 as traders were reluctant to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  too high.   \par \par \uc2 However, with the Bank Of Japan leaving interest rates unchanged Friday, renewed demand for carry trade saw the Kiwi pushed over the weekend.   \par \par \uc2 New Zealand's interest rates - the second highest in the developed world after Iceland - have attracted inflows in carry trade, when investors borrow in low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the yen, to invest in high-yielding ones.   \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ has said that it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unjustifiably high and when conditions are opportune. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when carried out, would also have to meet its inflation targeting regime.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week said that its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't prejudice the future direction of monetary policy.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -Shri Navaratnam, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; shri.navaratnam@dowjones.com \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 17-06-07 2235GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070617e36h000fi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
